v2.0.0 rebuilt the Baccarat module as a local Python server application. v2.1.0-v2.4.0 added the Tie
bet and its own stake, the half-screen layout, PASS recording the table's result, and the OCR
groundwork. v2.5.x-v2.7.x built and proved the OCR tooling, calibration, the confidence gate and the
live loop. v2.8.0 was the milestone: the reader read the user's live casino display correctly, and
found that a region containing the history grid and the balance row makes the model burn its whole
token budget.

v2.8.1 closed the "why is no result showing?" traps (a whole-screen region is refused at Start;
changing the profile while running is explained). v2.8.2 connects the setup screen to the reader — the
OCR profile now follows the session's provider and layout, so choosing "Pragmatic Half Width / Full
Length" at setup is the profile the reader uses — and makes Draw the region start from the table's
detected position instead of a guess, after a hand-drawn box landed on the chat panel twice. A
fallback model now covers the busy frames that occasionally defeat the fast one.

The per-release record for the module is BACARAT/CHANGELOG.md.
